    {
      "scope": "Offline 617.42 indexed DIFR first-field semantic qualification; no hardware or product edits.",
      "driver_sha256": "db407b964c11441642a1642a0922c35990de974c267a08537c3432765365f84b",
      "findings": [
        "Missing direct copy from registry group+B74/C7C to parent+974/+978 is an initialization-provenance gap. It is not by itself evidence that live controller10/11 first fields differ from controller0/4/12..15.",
        "DIFR controller identities are established separately by their source literals RMLpwrMsDifrSwAsrIdleThresholdUs and RMLpwrMsDifrCgIdleThresholdUs and existing individual-controller work. Default-generator switch 7372F0 selects parent+974 for index10 and +978 for index11; 737120 sends the selected value through the first member of its common converted pair, the same position used for other previously named controllers.",
        "E802 3A case 738B1F..B81 takes a single caller value, puts it in first pair member, zeros the second, and passes selected index r14d to 738200. 738200 uses the shared LPWR factor and checks the selected group row+F1 plus PMU capability before 73ACC0 transmits the same selected index and pair. There is an additional branch based on the selected row+F2 and associated callback; therefore this audit does not claim every controller takes identical auxiliary behavior.",
        "For the previously source-bound Blackwell provider, 738040 passes index unchanged to group virtual+98 -> B8FB80. That method reads each selected row hardware-ID byte at group+F0+index*108, rejects ID FF, and reads first and second indexed register-array DWORDs at 8F7100+4*ID and 8F7180+4*ID. It has no host index10/11 special-case for the two array selections. This is common host field routing, not proof of firmware receiver semantics or physical timing.",
        "Together the controller identity, common first-default-pair position, common selected-index 3A route and common raw provider support treating 10/11 first fields as the corresponding driver-requested DIFR idle thresholds under the same naming judgment used for other shipped controllers. This is an inference from source routing and names, not an independent specification of microseconds or a guarantee of firmware or physical behavior. Validate current support, hardware-ID/provider status, unique factor and exact selected/peer before-and-after readback on each adapter."
      ],
