    {
      "scope": "Offline bounded 3A auxiliary callback and controller row metadata audit; no hardware or product edits.",
      "driver_sha256": "db407b964c11441642a1642a0922c35990de974c267a08537c3432765365f84b",
      "findings": [
        "7388E0 obtains auxiliary object from [GPU+2550]+12C8 and selected row group+index*108. 738B1F calls 8F5980(aux,row+F2) when aux exists, then calls 8F5CF0(aux,row+F2,2) only if predicate succeeds before converting and sending 3A.",
        "8F5980 returns false for auxiliary index >=11, otherwise tests that bit in aux+5C. 8F5CF0 rejects absent/disabled entries, sets reason bit2 at aux+index*80+68, and if the prior reason DWORD was zero calls B9C340 to send firmware request 00/03/0D; for index1 there is also a virtual +598 invocation before that send. If reason DWORD was already nonzero, bit2 is set without that first-transition firmware send. Threshold restore alone does not establish that this auxiliary bit was cleared.",
        "736DB0 initializes controller row+F0 DWORD to 040B00FF, so byte F2 starts 0B. Its indexed switch cases for controller10 at 736FA3 and 11 at 736FBF do not replace byte+F2; 8F5980 rejects 0B, hence the source-defined initialized route for 10/11 skips this callback. This conclusion is scoped to the inspected construction and known handler paths, not a claim of immutable state forever. By contrast selected construction assigns index0->0, index4->2, index12->4, index13->5, index14->7, index15->6. Their callback depends on aux existence and presence bitmap; do not assume it is absent.",
        "8F59B0 creates the auxiliary object via 17F6850 and stores it at parent+12C8. Constructor trampoline 17F66B0 maps to metadata class ID 2B76B1; no authoritative class name was found. Same initializer reads literal RMAdaptivePwrDebug into object+60 and intersects it with object+5C, supporting an adaptive-power association but not a complete policy/firmware meaning.",
        "A801 type3 getter 738410..7387F4 and inspected delegated 738E20 do not directly expose row+F2 or the auxiliary reason DWORD. No independent getter or universal proof against future writers is claimed."
      ],
